# Persistence

- Each entity has a `DbSet` in its DbContext (`Persistence/Contexts`), an `IEntityTypeConfiguration<TEntity>` in
  `Persistence/EntityConfigurations` and a repository in `Persistence/Repositories`. nArchGen adds all three with
  `generate crud`.
- Repositories derive from `EfRepositoryBase<TEntity, TId, TContext>` and implement the interface in
  `Application/Services/Repositories`. Register new ones in `PersistenceServiceRegistration.cs`.
- Entity configurations set the table name, column names and the soft delete query filter
  (`HasQueryFilter(e => !e.DeletedDate.HasValue)`); keep the filter on every entity.
- Use the repository methods (`GetAsync`, `GetListAsync`, `AnyAsync`, …) from the Application layer; do not use the
  DbContext outside Persistence.
